 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Per-update complexity is $O(1)$ per active Gaussian parameter, similar to Adam. However, BOGausS requires maintaining per-Gaussian state variables ($t, \widehat{g}, \widehat{g}^2$), increasing memory overhead compared to a global optimizer state.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot D)$ where $N$ is the number of Gaussians and $D$ is the dimensionality of the parameters being optimized. This is significantly higher than standard Adam which might share state or use sparse updates if implemented naively, but BOGausS explicitly tracks state per Gaussian to ensure unbiasedness for sparse updates [S1].
